      "problem": "Evaluate the following product.\n\n$(-7\\,\\text{i})\\cdot (-8\\,\\text{i})=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Multiplying two purely imaginary numbers is similar to multiplying two monomials. We also use the fact that ${i}^{2}=-1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7\\,\\text{i})\\cdot (-8\\,\\text{i}) & =(-7)\\cdot (-8)\\cdot {\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =56\\,{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =56\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-56.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
